cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "pathway-stratification-validity: measuring whether annotation-derived gene set scores are reliable enough to rank individuals"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for evaluating gene set scores as reflective measurement scales for
  individual-level stratification. Condition effects and individual-level coherence are
  scored separately, each as an excess over size- and expression-matched random gene sets,
  so that a set which responds to a perturbation is not mistaken for one that ranks people
  reliably. Includes the negative-control machinery, the attribution of apparent coherence
  to the dominant expression axis of each cohort, test-retest reliability against matched
  controls, and the sensitivity analyses that vary the null model, the definition of
  coherence, the redundancy of the sets and the preprocessing.
